on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]provider-disable-core[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]provider-disable-core: add a versioned, lock-bounded, atomic [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]multi-provider disable store and PyO3 bindings in the linked sase-core [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]repo, then add the strict Python facade and lock-free display peek in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase. Cover concurrent entries, replacement, exact expiry, until-cleared[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]state, partial corruption cleanup, and binding parity.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make every model-selection path honor disabled providers[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]routing-semantics[dim] · [dim][/dim]after provider-disable-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]routing-semantics: introduce one routing-availability seam and apply it [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]to alias pools, ordered fallbacks, temporary alias overrides, default [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]autodetection, provider dispatch, model pickers, and completion [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]catalogs. Preserve direct-selection diagnostics, selector cursor [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]invariants, and automatic restoration on expiry.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Build the Provider Routing experience in the Models panel[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]models-panel-ux[dim] · [dim][/dim]after routing-semantics[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]models-panel-ux: add a provider-routing modal, duration and exact-time [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]flows, live countdown/status rendering, background refreshes, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]affected-alias presentation, a top-bar disabled-provider pill, keyboard [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]help, focused interaction tests, and PNG snapshots at normal and narrow [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]terminal sizes.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Document, stress, and land the combined provider-disable [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]feature[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]integration-and-docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after models-panel-ux[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]integration-and-docs: reconcile cross-phase behavior, update the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]LLM/ACE/Rust-backend docs, run the full sase-core and sase verification [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lanes including visual snapshots, and exercise expiry, fallback, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]direct-request, and multi-process state transitions in an end-to-end [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]smoke matrix before landing.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-mc","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-mc.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-11ed2a9cefe409b0f1ef994408866efe","started_at":"2026-08-15T15:13:42.206184+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[{"committed_at":1786814999,"sha":"58b9b447fed9d5bc4d7d637fbf428aea43b0f9f0","subject":"feat(llm-provider): honor disabled providers in model routing"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"8291038cd9661c5505cb1149098889906a06a7b1b1980ddf3ee7aa7a9a1634c6","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-mc.2/chat.md","size_bytes":32271},"commits":{"digest":"eb69a76f38ceb5ae3e3655cb1d5b56063888267df3932a9c1c4aa739c5c455b3","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-mc.2/commits.json","size_bytes":239},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"a398c70160fe308637edd70b38d8cf02cc697183c480675d10f387d529663058","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-mc.2/embedded_workflows.json","size_bytes":80},"meta":{"digest":"bfa304f5467d499eb0ff82201b7bd5692fe1df51a35b8f4e777440175d95592e","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-mc.2/meta.json","size_bytes":633},"prompt":{"digest":"d42c38d2d9e5cec4807bc8650fda7b6d957cc607bdeab77f1d57b36821c865d6","path":"a